    <innerclass refid="classhorus__human__core_1_1CalibrationPlugin" prot="public">horus_human_core::CalibrationPlugin</innerclass>
    <innernamespace refid="namespacehorus__human__core">horus_human_core</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Abstract calibration algorithm loaded by a HORUS channel node via pluginlib. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A channel node (horus_imu, horus_insole, horus_emg, ...) owns the data flow, the files and the ROS interfaces; the plugin owns only the math. During a calibration run the node feeds raw samples of the units being calibrated to add(); finish() turns them into a YAML result; load() applies a result (fresh or from file); apply() corrects every live sample. Swapping the algorithm is a one-line change of <computeroutput>calibration.plugin</computeroutput> in the node&apos;s YAML.</para>
<para>Threading: the node serialises every call under one mutex, so plugins need no locking. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
